// To change the wording, edit the text between the tags below.
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { url } from '../lib/urls';
---
<Base title="Resume | Brewster Smyers">
  <section class="page-heading wrap">
    <p class="eyebrow">Experience + education</p>
    <h1>Brewster Smyers<span>.</span></h1>
    <p>Mechanical engineering student · Bucknell University · Expected May 2028</p>
    <a class="button" href={url('resume/Brewster_Smyers_Resume.pdf')} download>Download resume PDF <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a>
  </section>

  <section class="resume-layout wrap">
    {/* Left column: quick facts */}
    <aside>
      <p class="eyebrow">At a glance</p>
      <p>B.S. Mechanical Engineering</p>
      <p>Minors in Mathematics and Business Analytics</p>
      <p>Marblehead, Massachusetts</p>
      <a class="text-link" href={url('contact/')}>Contact ↗</a>
    </aside>

    {/* Right column: the resume itself */}
    <article class="prose">
      <h2>Education</h2>
      <p>Bucknell University, B.S. Mechanical Engineering, expected May 2028. Minors in Mathematics and Business Analytics.</p>
      <p>Relevant coursework: Manufacturing Processes, Fluid Mechanics, Thermodynamics, Dynamics, Differential Equations, Probability and Statistics, Spreadsheet Modeling and Data Analysis. Spring 2027: SQL, Cloud Data Analytics and Generative AI; Financial Decision Modeling using Spreadsheets.</p>

      <h2>Technical skills</h2>
      <p><strong>CAD and simulation:</strong> SolidWorks (CSWA certified), SolidWorks Simulation (FEA), hand stress calculations.</p>
      <p><strong>Manufacturing:</strong> Mastercam, CNC milling (Haas), G-code, process planning, injection and compression molds, casting, 3D printing.</p>
      <p><strong>Programming and data:</strong> MATLAB, Python, Java, Arduino (C++), Excel spreadsheet modeling and data analysis.</p>

      <h2>Engineering projects</h2>
      <h3><a href={url('projects/ack-coaster-mold/')}>Injection Mold for Coaster</a></h3>
      <p>Manufacturing Processes, Fall 2026. Designed a coaster and its drafted aluminum injection mold in SolidWorks and wrote the approved process plan. Programmed the Mastercam toolpaths (5 tools, 880 lines of G-code), using rest machining to limit small-cutter time. The mold was CNC machined on a Haas mill from my code.</p>
      <h3><a href={url('projects/micro-drone-chassis/')}>Compression-Molded Micro-Drone Chassis</a></h3>
      <p>Personal project, Fall 2026 to present. Designed a 102 mm quadcopter frame and a 3D-printed split mold in SolidWorks to press it from chopped carbon. Molded the first carbon chassis in November 2026; next, testing it against 3D-printed frames of the same shape.</p>
      <h3><a href={url('projects/autonomous-underwater-vehicle/')}>Underwater Vehicle and Water Tunnel</a></h3>
      <p>Team lead, Fluid Mechanics, Fall 2026 to present. Leading a six-person team designing an unmanned underwater vehicle hull and a water tunnel to test a 100 mm scale model, with the work split so each member owns a subsystem. Designed the acrylic water tunnel in SolidWorks and did the hull hydrostatics by hand (267 N buoyancy, 1.1 m hull).</p>
      <h3><a href={url('projects/pipe-brace-bracket/')}>Pipe Brace Bracket FEA</a></h3>
      <p>Personal project, November 2026. Ran a static FEA of a welded steel pipe bracket at 1,000 N in SolidWorks Simulation and validated the 140 MPa bend stress by hand (factor of safety about 1.6). Traced a 376 MPa peak to a sharp-corner artifact and recommended a 700 N limit or a gusset and heavier pipe.</p>
      <h3><a href={url('projects/outdoor-landmark-chair/')}>Outdoor Landmark Chair</a></h3>
      <p>Personal project, October 2025. Designed an 8 ft braced-frame chair in SolidWorks with a stress study and built it alone in 2 days for about $1,000. It seats four to five people and is still in use.</p>

      <h2>Leadership</h2>
      <h3>Organizer · Movember Charity Triathlon</h3>
      <p>Bucknell University, November 2026. Planning an indoor triathlon for men's mental health (venue, risk, waivers, volunteers); raised $850+.</p>
      <h3>Infrastructure and Social Chair · Sigma Phi Epsilon</h3>
      <p>Designed and built modular risers, seating and stages; planned events for 100+ attendees.</p>

      <h2>Work experience</h2>
      <h3>Bartender · The Nantucket Hotel & Resort (2026); The Landing, Marblehead (2022–2025)</h3>
      <p>Ran a 13-seat bar and worked high-volume weddings and events, coordinating with kitchen and floor staff.</p>

      <h2>Activities</h2>
      <p>Founder, club Ultimate Frisbee · About 200 miles of the Appalachian Trail (Camp Kieve) · Skiing, cycling, hiking</p>

      <p class="muted">The PDF is the full one-page résumé.</p>
    </article>
